.SH "NAME"
pcre2_set_optimize \- set an optimization directive
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.sp
.ss \n[.ss]
.nf
.fam C
\f(CR\&#include <pcre2.h>

int\fP \f(CBpcre2_set_optimize\fP\f(CR(pcre2_compile_context *\fP\f(CIccontext\fP\f(CR,
                       uint32_t\fP \f(CIdirective\fP\f(CR);\fP
.fam
.fi
.ss \n[.ss] 0
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.sp
This function controls which performance optimizations will be applied
by \f(CBpcre2_compile()\fP. It can be called multiple times with the same compile
context; the effects are cumulative, with the effects of later calls taking
precedence over earlier ones.
.sp
The result is zero for success, \f(CBPCRE2_ERROR_NULL\fP if \f(CIccontext\fP is \f(CBNULL\fP,
or \f(CBPCRE2_ERROR_BADOPTION\fP if \f(CIdirective\fP is unknown. The latter could be
useful to detect if a certain optimization is available.
.sp
The list of possible values for the \f(CIdirective\fP parameter are:
.sp
.RS 4
.PD 0
.TP 25
\f(CBPCRE2_OPTIMIZATION_FULL\fP
.ad l
Enable all optimizations (default)
.TP 25
\f(CBPCRE2_OPTIMIZATION_NONE\fP
.ad l
Disable all optimizations
.TP 25
\f(CBPCRE2_AUTO_POSSESS\fP
.ad l
Enable auto\-possessification
.TP 25
\f(CBPCRE2_AUTO_POSSESS_OFF\fP
.ad l
Disable auto\-possessification
.TP 25
\f(CBPCRE2_DOTSTAR_ANCHOR\fP
.ad l
Enable implicit dotstar anchoring
.TP 25
\f(CBPCRE2_DOTSTAR_ANCHOR_OFF\fP
.ad l
Disable implicit dotstar anchoring
.TP 25
\f(CBPCRE2_START_OPTIMIZE\fP
.ad l
Enable start\-up optimizations at match time
.TP 25
\f(CBPCRE2_START_OPTIMIZE_OFF\fP
.ad l
Disable start\-up optimizations at match time
.PD
.RE
.PP
.ad l
.sp
There is a complete description of the PCRE2 native API, including detailed
